{% extends '_article.jinja' %}
{% from 'data/pages.jinja' import catalogue %}
{% set article = catalogue['design'] %}
{% block article_body %}
<section aria-labelledby="identity"><h2 id="identity">Lattice, material, instrument</h2>
<p>The lattice mark suggests an anomalous node. Carbon carries the cover; alumina carries reading. Teal marks instrument views and links; amber marks transported records and dark-surface focus.</p><div class="fl-swatches"><div class="fl-swatch-carbon"><strong>Carbon</strong>Cover and code</div><div><strong>Alumina</strong>Reading surface</div><div class="fl-swatch-teal"><strong>Teal</strong>Instrument</div><div class="fl-swatch-amber"><strong>Amber</strong>Transport</div></div><p>IBM Plex Sans carries the prose and display hierarchy. IBM Plex Mono carries code and catalogue metadata. Light-surface links use an ink teal with sufficient contrast; luminous teal belongs on carbon.</p>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="cast"><h2 id="cast">Catalogue the residents</h2>
{{ ui.figure('anchor-habitat', 'A ceramic capybara rests beside a circular buffer while a long-neck robotic dinosaur examines an interface bridge.', '05', 'Queue occupancy continues to rise. The capybara remains seated.') }}<ul><li>Panda: record transport and handoff.</li><li>Capybara: queues, batching, and back-pressure.</li><li>Dinosaur: compatibility and interface continuity.</li></ul><p>Animals do not replace API names, error messages, or technical diagrams. Every survey image is labelled as fictional scientific illustration. Apparent femtoscale machinery is worldbuilding, not physical evidence.</p>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="specimens"><h2 id="specimens">Component and asset specimens</h2>
<div class="fl-actions">{{ ui.button('Primary action', '/femtologging/getting-started/') }}{{ ui.button('Secondary action', '/femtologging/docs/', true) }}</div><p>These links demonstrate the visual system and lead to real site pages. Native disclosure keeps supplementary information available without scripting.</p><details><summary>Read the caption grammar</summary><p>Figure number, specimen ID, fictional context, then one observed action. The caption stays in HTML; the raster carries no labels or measurements.</p></details><p><a href="/femtologging/assets/logos/lockup-carbon.svg" download>Download the lattice wordmark</a> · <a href="/femtologging/assets/icons/sprite.svg" download>Download the SVG icon set</a> · <a href="/femtologging/assets/fonts/sans-LICENSE.txt">Sans font licence</a> · <a href="/femtologging/assets/fonts/mono-LICENSE.txt">Mono font licence</a></p>
</section>
{% endblock %}
